`HTTP_ADDR` defaults to `127.0.0.1:8080`. This baseline has no authentication,
authorization, persistence, or message transport. Do not expose it publicly as-is.
`/healthz` is a liveness check, not dependency readiness.

Business modules live in `internal/<module>`. Their nested `internal` packages are
implementation details. Operations are direct typed calls; constructors and wiring
are explicit. `AGENTS.md` and `gsvc contract --json` describe the supported workflow.

`gsvc add` is idempotent for identical requests. It preserves developer-owned files
and refuses edits to existing managed output. `--dry-run --json` plans without
writing. `--expect <plan-id>` prevents applying a stale review. `gsvc sync` can
recreate missing managed output, but does not bless edited generated files.

Files labeled developer-owned are editable; generated files and contracts are not.
The ownership map is `.gsvc/ownership.json`. Commit it alongside `gsvc.json`.

Use a currently supported Go toolchain. The generated language floor is Go 1.23.
Configure CI to install the exact CLI version from a trusted release/source commit
before running `gsvc check --verify --strict`; make this check required for merges.
